{'symbol': 'CAT', 'date': '2020-07-31 08:30:00', 'title': 'CATERPILLAR REPORTS Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.84', 'text': "CATERPILLAR REPORTS SECOND-QUARTER 2020 RESULTS.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.84.Q2 SALES $10 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $9.38 BILLION.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.64 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.NOT PROVIDING A FINANCIAL OUTLOOK FOR 2020 AT THIS TIME..FINANCIAL RESULTS FOR REMAINDER OF 2020 WILL BE IMPACTED BY CONTINUED GLOBAL ECONOMIC UNCERTAINTY DUE TO COVID-19 PANDEMIC.AS OF MID-JULY 2020, GLOBALLY AND ACROSS 3 PRIMARY SEGMENTS, NEARLY ALL PRIMARY PRODUCTION FACILITIES CONTINUED TO OPERATE.CATERPILLAR - DEALERS DECREASED MACHINE AND ENGINE INVENTORIES ABOUT $1.4 BILLION DURING Q2 2020, COMPARED WITH INCREASE OF ABOUT $500 MILLION DURING Q2 2019.EXPENSE FOR CORPORATE ITEMS AND ELIMINATIONS WAS $580 MILLION IN Q2 OF 2020, AN INCREASE OF $89 MILLION FROM Q2 OF 2019.DECLINE IN QTRLY SALES WAS DUE TO LOWER SALES VOLUME DRIVEN BY LOWER END-USER DEMAND AND IMPACT FROM CHANGES IN DEALER INVENTORIES.AT THE END OF Q2, PAST DUES AT CAT FINANCIAL WERE 3.74%, VERSUS 3.38% AT THE END OF Q2 OF 2019.AS OF JUNE 30, CAT FINANCIAL'S ALLOWANCE FOR CREDIT LOSSES TOTALED $515 MILLION, VERSUS $457 MILLION AT MARCH 31."}